From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 00:41:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05393/11362] [outer-loop] pre-stage .472: energy-based ARC
 research lineup (5 tasks), reversing the PHASE-D-majority allocation

Operator: 'we want to continue down this energy based models path for
ARC-AGI-3, and tackle the multi-level capable live agent. what research
should we line up next?' then 'pre-stage the roadmap for all 5.'

research-roadmap-next.yaml, milestone 2026.07.472, 6 tasks (1 transition +
5 research). Investigated current state before drafting rather than working
from stale memory: reproducible_total_levels flat at 69 since the 6/30
pivot; selection/value-head axis genuinely exhausted (5 sub-hypotheses
nulled, confirmed as recently as 7/1); but TWO genuinely positive results
(exp4245 ARC oracle-distinct win +44.2pp, GAP-4 calibrated first positive)
were never nulled -- just abandoned mid-protocol when the pivot hit.
Also found DiffusionGemma's 'stays gated' status is based on a MuSR-domain
null (D1), not a retest of exp4245's actual ARC-domain claim -- possible
premise conflation, same error class as the FoVer retraction.

5 tasks: exp5151 hardens exp4245 (multiseed/leak-audit/cross-game, reusing
GAP-4's protocol shape); exp5152 resolves whether the DiffusionGemma gate
is well-founded or conflates domains; exp5153 executes GAP-4's own already-
documented forward protocol verbatim; exp5154 is the novel piece -- energy-
as-fitness generation-time guidance (QD search using Carnot's actual energy
machinery, not a novelty bonus or symbolic filter) attacking the diagnosed
GENERATION wall directly, citing .432's two directed-exploration nulls
(exp4688/4689) with an explicit distinction of what's genuinely different
this time; exp5155 scopes (not builds) the separate multi-level/deepen wall.

Validated before committing: YAML valid; exclusion_manifest_lint.py exit 0
(1 WARNING with valid operator_override on the routine transition task, 0
HARD after honestly citing exp5151's 4 matched priors as precondition
BLOCKS rather than methodology failures -- retire_if_same_verdict=false on
all 4, since a fixed-and-retried precondition isn't a doomed rerun);
arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py exit 0 (1 level-up attempt, satisfies the
Level-Up Attempt Guarantee); milestone field matches
_expected_next_milestone('2026.07.471') exactly, so the Pre-Staged Roadmap
Convention will preserve this file and skip the planner.

